---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import CtaPair from "../components/CtaPair.astro";
import FinalCta from "../components/FinalCta.astro";
import PageHero from "../components/PageHero.astro";

const title = "Lead Follow-Up and Review Automation | Launchline Design";
const description =
  "Missed-call text-back, Google review requests, reminders, and speed-to-lead follow-up for Miami businesses. Starter is $497 setup and $197 a month.";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="Starter, plus add-ons"
    title="Follow-up that goes out before the lead goes cold."
    lede="Instant lead follow-up, reminders, review requests, and a shared inbox. Starter catches the missed call. Add-ons cover the web form, the no-show, and the customer who went quiet."
    crumbs={[
      { href: "/", label: "Home" },
      { href: "/automation", label: "Automation" },
    ]}
  >
    <CtaPair loomHref="/demo#custom-demo" />
  </PageHero>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="wrap cards">
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Included in Starter</p>
        <h3>Missed-call text-back</h3>
        <p>The moment a call to your business line goes unanswered, a text goes out in the voice you approved. The thread lives in one inbox on web and mobile.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Included in Starter</p>
        <h3>Review requests</h3>
        <p>After a job or visit, a Google review request sends itself. You are not chasing five-star asks from the truck.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Included in Starter</p>
        <h3>Scripts and a monthly tune-up</h3>
        <p>Message copy is written for your brand, not a generic blast. Once a month we look at what people actually replied and adjust.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Add-on · $497 + $97/mo</p>
        <h3>Speed-to-lead</h3>
        <p>Web forms and ads get a reply while the lead is still on the page, not the next morning.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Add-on · $297 + $47/mo</p>
        <h3>Reminders and no-shows</h3>
        <p>Appointment reminders, then a follow-up when someone does not arrive. Useful for dental, med spas, and booked service windows.</p>
      </article>
      <article class="panel">
        <p class="eyebrow">Add-on · $750 once</p>
        <h3>Reactivation</h3>
        <p>A past-customer campaign, scoped once, for the list you already have. Not an ongoing blast you forget to turn off.</p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" style="padding-top: 0">
    <div class="wrap prose">
      <h2>Starter is the on-ramp. It is not the whole system.</h2>
      <p>
        Starter is $497 to set up and $197 a month. It is built for owner-operators — roofing, HVAC, pest control — who miss calls while they are on the job. There is a free 14-day pilot: we set Starter up on your line at no cost, and you keep it only if it is catching calls you would have missed.
      </p>
      <p>
        When you want the phone answered out loud, that is <a href="/ai-receptionist">Growth</a>, which includes every Starter automation. When the follow-up has to cross a CRM, a practice system, or a bilingual intake flow, that is <a href="/custom-ai">Custom</a>. A single custom automation, outside the packages, starts at $750.
      </p>
      <p>
        Usage for SMS and AI is billed at cost with no markup. Your number and your customer replies stay in accounts you own.
      </p>
      <p>Most Starter setups go live in as little as 7 days, after you approve every script.</p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <FinalCta />
</Base>
